## What's new & how to use it

### 1. Crisp expand/collapse icons
- The old `🗖/🗕` are replaced with **custom SVG icons** that clearly show an arrow pointing **out (expand)** or **in (collapse)**.
- Works reliably on all modern browsers – no more mysterious boxed `[X]`.

### 2. Picture‑in‑picture of the watched stream
- Click the **📺 PiP** button in the toolbar.
- A small 200×112px YouTube player appears **bottom‑right of your camera preview**.
- It plays the exact same video you’re watching on the left – muted and without controls.
- **Your own broadcast preview now contains that tiny video**, exactly as your viewers would see when you capture the window.
- Click the **✕** button on the PiP to close it, or toggle the PiP button again.

### 3. Why this is powerful
- When you screen‑share or capture this browser window with OBS, the PiP stays on top of your camera feed – so **your audience always sees what you’re reacting to**.
- You can still expand either chat independently, just like before.

